        "id": 239618,
        "name": "Sea-Envy",
        "username": "Sea-Envy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/sea-envy/{size}/1849_2.png",
        "created_at": "2021-07-27T21:47:57.682Z",
        "cooked": "<p>So for the adventure i am trying to write for tis weekend there will be a attempted bank robbery with the super villains escaping to be tracked back to their lair for a harder fight. (like you do)</p>\n<p>What is the best/most fair way to run this?<br>\nLet them all got to 0 health and then say “but then they escape”<br>\nhave them flee when at &gt;10 health?<br>\nsome other option?</p>\n<p>this bad guy group have deception/ misdirection schtick so i would not feel as bad about “you did everything right and thought you won but no” but still it seems a not great thing to do as a GM</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-07-27T21:47:57.682Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 43,
        "reads": 30,
        "readers_count": 29,
        "score": 216.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 28706,
        "topic_slug": "and-the-villain-escapes",
        "display_username": "Sea-Envy",
        "primary_group_name": null,
        "flair_name": null,
        "flair_url": null,
        "flair_bg_color": null,
        "flair_color": null,
        "flair_group_id": null,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
