      {
        "id": 239620,
        "name": "",
        "username": "fjur",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/fjur/{size}/4849_2.png",
        "created_at": "2021-07-27T23:58:19.904Z",
        "cooked": "<p>You could have the Villain make one or more Overcome Actions to get away. The Villain could have Minions that Boost the Villain, and Heroes could Hinder the Villain or Attack those Minions to give them the illusion that they can stop the Villain’s escape.</p>\n<p>So, the encounter could end in one of several ways:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>The Scene Tracker runs out or the Villain succeeds on enough Overcomes without any Twists.</li>\n<li>The Villain succeeds on enough Overcomes with some Minor Twists.</li>\n<li>The Villain succeeds on enough Overcomes with some more Major Twists.</li>\n<li>The Villain is reduced to some Health threshold (such as 10 or 0).</li>\n</ol>\n<p>In all cases, the Villain would escape, of course (because that’s what The Plot needs to happen). However, the Heroes can still influence <em>how</em> the Villain makes its escape. The higher the method of escape is numbered, the worse the Villain’s escape is. Depending on how the Villain gets away, you can make the lair fight easier, make tracking the Villain easier, or make the Villain have to leave some (or all) of the loot behind.</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-07-27T23:58:19.904Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
